[COMMENTS]
STATION,Crump weir gauging a Chalk rural catchment with some artificial influences, station reconstructed in 1979. GENERAL: Crump profile weir, 6m broad. Prior to Oct 1979, broad-crested weir (crest: 7.4m), situated under double-arch bridge. STATION HYDROMETRY: Two peak flow ratings applied across period of record, the most recent is valid from October-1979. Current rating only reliable to bankfull. Dredging increased modular limit. Theoretical rating for original weir confirmed by c/m measurements. Part of the Thet-Little Ouse groundwater support scheme, which triggers at 350 l/s to maintain flow. These trigger flows apply when the scheme is being used as a river support scheme for water users (not for Ely Ouse to Essex Transfer Scheme). The amount pumped in any one season is initially limited to 3 per cent of the annual licenced quantity of the Thet-Little Ouse scheme. FLOW RECORD: Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2019 (WINFAP Files v8). FLOW REGIME: Regime influenced by groundwater abstraction/recharge. Abstractions for industry and agriculture. Some effluent returns.
CATCHMENT,Chalk with large Boulder Clay cover. Rural catchment, arable with some forest and grassland, several small towns.
Qmed Suitability,Gauged above QMED. Weir remains modular with good fit to gaugings.
Pooling Suitability,Weir becomes non-modular which is not accounted for in current rating.
[END]
